# A lead who changes their mind AT the readback.
#
# This satisfied neither arm of the old P7 branch: the elif required a confirm, so a lead
# proposing a different time was ignored entirely — `accepted_slot` kept the old value and
# `slot_status` still said "accepted" for the time they had just rejected. Roma would then
# read that same time back again.
#
# The ordering trap is the reason this script exists. Turn 4's reply opens with "haan", and
# `is_affirmation` fires on "haan" — so a confirm-first ordering LOCKS the old slot and
# reports a win against a booking the lead declined. Revision must be checked first.
#
# The visit still locks at the end, on the REVISED slot. A revision is not a refusal.
